1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,083
Medieval life: old at 30.

2
00:00:03,233 --> 00:00:05,650
Except... not really.

3
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:08,317
Dead at 30? The average trick.

4
00:00:08,467 --> 00:00:11,783
Life expectancy was around 30.

5
00:00:11,933 --> 00:00:13,983
But that's an average.

6
00:00:14,133 --> 00:00:17,450
And many babies didn't make it to 5.

7
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:20,450
That drags the average way down.

8
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:23,717
One baby. One 60-year-old.

9
00:00:23,867 --> 00:00:26,250
Average age: 30.

10
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,783
Neither died at 30.

11
00:00:28,933 --> 00:00:32,650
Make it to adulthood, and you'd often see 50.

12
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:35,350
Or 60. Or 70.

13
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:37,850
Plenty of grandparents.

14
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,117
Queen Eleanor of Aquitaine lived to about 80.

15
00:00:42,267 --> 00:00:44,317
So why the myth?

16
00:00:44,467 --> 00:00:47,683
People read the average as a lifespan.

17
00:00:47,833 --> 00:00:49,883
Two different numbers.

18
00:00:50,033 --> 00:00:53,550
Average: 30. Adults: much older.

19
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:56,317
Dead at 30: not the rule.

20
00:00:56,467 --> 00:01:00,450
Anyway, here's a medieval peasant at 30.
